# Byteman rules for MAX_HINT_BUFFERS-switchCurrentBuffer-MAX_ALLOCATED_BUFFERS, §9d.
# Observation only: they change no behaviour, they write two kinds of trace line.
#
#   created=<allocatedBuffers> size=<bufferSize> max=<MAX_ALLOCATED_BUFFERS> ms=<epoch millis> thread=<name>
#       one line per buffer the pool creates, written at the exit of
#       HintsBufferPool.createBuffer() (HintsBufferPool.java:130-134). The number
#       of lines is the usage counter: the pool exposes no gauge for it. The
#       first line on an idle node comes from the hints executor's periodic
#       flush, not from a writer (case 9d).
#
#   waiting ms=<epoch millis> thread=<name>
#       one line per entry into the disallow branch, written at the
#       BlockingQueue.take invocation in switchCurrentBuffer() (line 118) —
#       the same location HintsBufferPoolTest's rule uses.
#
# Output file: the system property stage4.byteman.out, or else hints-pool.txt in
# the JVM's working directory. Both rules share it.
#
# Loaded at node start with -javaagent:<byteman.jar>=script:<this file>,listener:true
# (case 9e), or attached to the unit test with -Dtest.jvm.args.

RULE hints pool creates a buffer
CLASS org.apache.cassandra.hints.HintsBufferPool
METHOD createBuffer
AT EXIT
IF true
DO traceOpen("hintsPool", java.lang.System.getProperty("stage4.byteman.out", "hints-pool.txt"));
   traceln("hintsPool", "created=" + $0.allocatedBuffers + " size=" + $0.bufferSize + " max=" + org.apache.cassandra.hints.HintsBufferPool.MAX_ALLOCATED_BUFFERS + " ms=" + java.lang.System.currentTimeMillis() + " thread=" + java.lang.Thread.currentThread().getName())
ENDRULE

RULE hints pool writer waits at the cap
CLASS org.apache.cassandra.hints.HintsBufferPool
METHOD switchCurrentBuffer
AT INVOKE java.util.concurrent.BlockingQueue.take
IF true
DO traceOpen("hintsPool", java.lang.System.getProperty("stage4.byteman.out", "hints-pool.txt"));
   traceln("hintsPool", "waiting ms=" + java.lang.System.currentTimeMillis() + " thread=" + java.lang.Thread.currentThread().getName())
ENDRULE
